  "headline": "Gateway to the Himalayas",
  "short_description": "Manali, in the Kullu Valley, is a base for Himalayan adventure sports, snow-capped views and the Rohtang/Atal Tunnel route to Lahaul-Spiti.",
  "about": "Set beside the Beas river in the Kullu Valley, Manali has grown from a quiet Himalayan village into one of North India's most popular hill destinations for adventure and honeymoon travel.\n\nLocated in the Kullu Valley of Himachal Pradesh, on the banks of the Beas river, at the base of the Pir Panjal range.\n\nA blend of Himachali Pahari traditions and a large backpacker/adventure-tourism culture, especially around Old Manali.\n\nPredominantly Hindu, with landmark temples like Hidimba Devi; also a base for visiting Buddhist monasteries en route to Lahaul-Spiti.",
  "history": "Named after the sage Manu in local legend; historically a trade route town connecting India to Ladakh and Central Asia via ancient passes.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Kullu-Manali Airport (airport, ~50 km)\n- Joginder Nagar (railway)\n- Manali Bus Stand (HRTC) (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Pahari, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "March to June, and October to February for snow",
  "ideal_duration_text": "3–4 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Kullu-Manali Airport, Bhuntar (KUU), ~50 km away",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Joginder Nagar (narrow gauge, limited) / Chandigarh for broad-gauge and flights",
